      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LUX AETERNA (8) returns to Sydney after a Group 1 second in Brisbane last week, finishing by 2.4m off glamour mare Eye Keep Smiling in the Golden Girl. Draws much wider but will enjoy the class drop and owns a strong strike rate at this circuit and distance. With even luck she is up to winning this. CAN BE A RUEBE NZ (5) could be a big danger in her first outing since May. She won twice at this circuit and distance last campaign along with a third in the Sibelia Stakes and a fifth in the G1 Queen Elizabeth II Mile, beating LUX AETERNA home both times. Yet to miss the first-three when fresh and will be ready to go off a trial win. JILLIBY ILLUMINATE NZ (4) couldn't match the boys last week but was runner-up in her four previous attempts against the mares at this venue and distance so is better placed. SWEET DREAMS NZ (2) draws lower than last week and had won her other three outings in Australia. ULTIMATE DIVA (3) came from wider when runner-up here last week and draws to be competitive.",
